{{!< default}}
{{!-- The tag above means: insert everything in this file into the body of the default.hbs template --}}

{{#post}}

{{!-- Historia Arcana: this template is a router.

     Commentarii Mundi reports get their own full layout; every other post renders
     the upstream Source article, unchanged. Ghost cannot select a template by
     tag — the only alternative is a custom-*.hbs template picked per post in the
     editor, which does not fit a backend that creates posts through the Admin API.

     The CM layout needs BOTH the #commentarii-mundi tag AND the published page with
     slug "commentarii-mundi" — that page is the master switch (see
     docs/commentarii-mundi.md §2). Either missing → the upstream article.

     The upstream article itself lives in
     partials/commentarii-mundi/source-article.hbs, because both branches need it.
     Upstream changes to post.hbs belong there. --}}

{{#has tag="#commentarii-mundi"}}
    {{#get "pages" filter="slug:commentarii-mundi" fields="id" limit="1" as |cmHome|}}
        {{#if cmHome}}
            {{> "commentarii-mundi/report" ../this}}
        {{else}}
            {{> "commentarii-mundi/source-article" ../this}}
        {{/if}}
    {{/get}}
{{else}}
    {{> "commentarii-mundi/source-article"}}
{{/has}}

{{/post}}
